== recursive navigation geometry (key insight) ==

the 8 missing corner subcubes of the node formation define a 10x10x10 central void.
void:group ratio = 1:2 (exact). zoom factor between scale levels = 2.
the x20 jump in scale constants = 2 (void ratio) x 10 (decimal/binary boundary).
corner nodes ARE the entry points — double-clicking one is geometrically meaningful.
at depth > 0: outer node group shown faintly at 0.2 opacity as spatial anchor.
data model: /orbital.json?context=NODE:X returns zenki list as known[] at level 1.

== key technical notes ==

- p7refToCoords decodes ADDR_B32: standard RFC4648 base32, chars A-Z2-7
  bytes: [theta/255*2pi, phi/255*pi, psi/255*pi, omega/255*2pi, 4-byte time_offset]
- fake node injection: perl -e to generate pkey_b32 + addr_b32, then p7c discover.inject-orbital
  example pkey: "IJBEEQSCIJBEEQSCIJBEEQSCIJBEEQSCIJBEEQSCIJBEEQSCIJBA"
  example p7ref: "NODE:NODEB00:FJKY2PYAAAAAA" (theta=60 phi=120 psi=200)
- Convert::Color::HSV must be explicitly autoloaded in graphics-matrix.init_code
  (unlike ticker which calls HSV->new directly at runtime triggering lazy load)
- kimi.connect: responded cache cleared on reconnect — double-approving is harmless,
  silent drops are not

